      "content": "The idea that certain races have inherently different pain thresholds is a dangerous myth often used to justify medical discrimination, but it is not scientifically supported.\nHowever, it is true that cultural differences in how patients from minority groups report pain or describe symptoms can lead to under-treatment if clinicians aren't careful.\nYou should focus on listening to the patient's specific description rather than relying on stereotypes about their race or biology.",
